#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "the bow turns one step."
msgstr "l'arc tourne d'un cran."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Edge knock"
msgstr "Butée"

msgid "Edge knock: the bow is turned as far as it goes."
msgstr "Butée : l'arc est tourné au maximum."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "the bow is turned as far as it goes."
msgstr "l'arc est tourné au maximum."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Empty quiver"
msgstr "Carquois vide"

msgid "Empty quiver: a hollow tap of wood."
msgstr "Carquois vide : un coup de bois creux."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a hollow tap of wood."
msgstr "un coup de bois creux."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Pop"
msgstr "Pop"

msgid "Pop: a paper heart bursts."
msgstr "Pop : un cœur en papier éclate."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a paper heart bursts."
msgstr "un cœur en papier éclate."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Sweetheart chord"
msgstr "Accord des amoureux"

msgid ""
"Sweetheart chord: rising chimes that end in a chord. Both hearts of a pair, "
"one after the other."
msgstr ""
"Accord des amoureux : des carillons qui montent et finissent en accord. Les "
"deux cœurs d'une paire, l'un après l'autre."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid ""
"rising chimes that end in a chord. Both hearts of a pair, one after the "
"other."
msgstr ""
"des carillons qui montent et finissent en accord. Les deux cœurs d'une "
"paire, l'un après l'autre."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Rose caught"
msgstr "Rose attrapée"

msgid "Rose caught: a rustle and a bright harp run."
msgstr "Rose attrapée : un froissement et une vive montée de harpe."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a rustle and a bright harp run."
msgstr "un froissement et une vive montée de harpe."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Golden heart caught"
msgstr "Cœur d'or attrapé"

msgid "Golden heart caught: a burst of bells, high and bright."
msgstr "Cœur d'or attrapé : une salve de clochettes, aiguës et vives."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a burst of bells, high and bright."
msgstr "une salve de clochettes, aiguës et vives."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Note caught"
msgstr "Billet attrapé"

msgid "Note caught: paper unfolding, and a soft chord. A love note to keep."
msgstr ""
"Billet attrapé : du papier qui se déplie, et un doux accord. Un billet doux "
"à garder."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "paper unfolding, and a soft chord. A love note to keep."
msgstr ""
"du papier qui se déplie, et un doux accord. Un billet doux à garder."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Miss"
msgstr "Raté"

msgid "Miss: a far tap on roof tiles. The arrow met nothing."
msgstr "Raté : un coup lointain sur les tuiles. La flèche n'a rien touché."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a far tap on roof tiles. The arrow met nothing."
msgstr "un coup lointain sur les tuiles. La flèche n'a rien touché."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Sights ping"
msgstr "Ping de visée"

msgid ""
"Sights ping: a small glassy ping. Let go now and the arrow meets a target."
msgstr ""
"Ping de visée : un petit ping de verre. Lâche maintenant et la flèche "
"atteint une cible."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a small glassy ping. Let go now and the arrow meets a target."
msgstr ""
"un petit ping de verre. Lâche maintenant et la flèche atteint une cible."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Rooftop bell"
msgstr "Cloche du toit"

msgid "Rooftop bell: a round begins."
msgstr "Cloche du toit : une manche commence."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "a round begins."
msgstr "une manche commence."

#. the name or the meaning of a longer line
msgid "Quiver spent"
msgstr "Carquois épuisé"

msgid "Quiver spent: three falling notes. The round is over."
msgstr "Carquois épuisé : trois notes qui descendent. La manche est finie."

